From 3aeb40930dfd88eee3894369aaddd3ebd2ab1243 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: AuraLite <auralite@example.invalid>
Date: Sun, 18 Oct 2026 15:55:46 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Post-audit fixes A1-A3: debugger linear address, alias
 warning, TAP port

A1: $rip is the raw instruction pointer while $lin is cs.base+rip; in real
mode they differ (reset vector: 0xfff0 vs 0xfffffff0), so 'x/i $rip' read
RAM instead of the ROM and displayed zeros.  cmd_regs now prints the linear
address beside the raw one, help documents the pair and when to use which,
and tests/test_dbg.c pins the arithmetic plus both x/i forms (including that
they disagree on purpose when the CS base is nonzero).  NC: without the lin
row the new vector reddens (RC measured).

A2: mem_init documents the one spatial surprise of this machine -- the
0xE0000-0xFFFFF alias lives INSIDE m->ram (m->rom keeps the pristine flash)
-- and that perf_tlb_plain_table() excludes the window for exactly that
reason, so future RAM-only caches must keep doing so.

A3: the net harnesses hard-bound the ground-rule TAP endpoint
(UDP 127.0.0.1:8080/8081/8082).  AURALITE_TAP_PORT now moves the whole
family (n2/n3 derive their NC lanes as +1/+2, responders get --port from
the lane endpoint), and n1 gains the D11 port-free pre-flight the other
two already had.  Defaults unchanged: n1/n2/n3 receipts byte-identical on
8080 and on a moved port (measured, ALL PASS).
